{
  "id": "s02-l03",
  "unit": "s02-consonants",
  "title": "Consonants 3: ট ঠ ড ঢ ণ",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Row 3 is the **retroflex** row: curl your tongue tip back and touch the ridge behind your teeth. **ট ঠ ড ঢ ণ**.\n\nGood news for English speakers: **English t and d are already close to ট and ড.** টাকা (`taka`, *taka/money*) and ডাক্তার (`daktar`, *doctor*) sound natural to you. ঠ and ঢ add a puff: ঠিক আছে (`thik achhe`, *OK*), ঢাকা (`dhaka`).\n\n**ঠ is not English 'th'.** It's a t with breath, like the t in *top* said forcefully.\n\n**ণ** sounds just like ন (`n`); learn it as 'the other n letter' (লবণ `lobon`, *salt*). Watch out: **ড** looks like the vowel **উ**, but ড has a notch in the top line.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "l-tta",
      "bn": "ট",
      "tr": "to",
      "en": "hard t, tongue curled back (like English 't' in 'top')",
      "notes": "Name: to (ট). Retroflex. English t is closer to ট than to ত."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-ttha",
      "bn": "ঠ",
      "tr": "tho",
      "en": "hard t with a puff of air (not English 'th')",
      "notes": "Name: tho (ঠ). Aspirated partner of ট."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-dda",
      "bn": "ড",
      "tr": "do",
      "en": "hard d, tongue curled back (like English 'd' in 'dog')",
      "notes": "Name: do (ড). Look-alike: উ (vowel) has no headline notch; ড has a notch on top. ড় (with a dot) is a different sound (s02-l07)."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-ddha",
      "bn": "ঢ",
      "tr": "dho",
      "en": "hard d with a breathy puff",
      "notes": "Name: dho (ঢ). First letter of ঢাকা."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-nna",
      "bn": "ণ",
      "tr": "n",
      "en": "n (same sound as ন; 'retroflex n' letter)",
      "notes": "Name: murdhonno no (মূর্ধন্য ণ). Sounds like ন today; the difference is spelling only. Rarely starts a word."
    },
    {
      "id": "dhol",
      "bn": "ঢোল",
      "tr": "dhol",
      "en": "drum (traditional)",
      "notes": "Two-headed folk drum played at weddings and Pohela Boishakh."
    }
  ],
